-- title:
--   Minimality of the Igusa branch at a crossing node
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and $M'\ge 1$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}=$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a nonunit of $A$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ an element lying in $A$, such that the contraction $A_0 = A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $(\pi_0)$, is Henselian, has algebraically closed residue field, and is such that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo $\mathfrak m_A$ to an element of $A_0$. Give `fieldBar q M'` (the intermediate field `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` of Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) its $k_0$-algebra structure. The assertion is then: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ and every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ whose contraction to $k_0$ is $A_0$, which is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$; for every subring $O \subseteq W_0$ of $F_0$ that is local and Noetherian, whose contraction to $k_0$ is $A_0$, such that every $f \in O$ differs from the image of some element of $A_0$ lying in $O$ by a nonunit of $O$, and such that every element of $F_0$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g, h \in O$, $h \neq 0$; for every $E_0 \ge 1$, with the image of $\pi_0$ lying in $O$, every $c_x, c_y \in O$, unit $u$ of $O$, ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the $\mathfrak m_O$-adic completion of $O$ onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` $\widehat{A_0}$ at $\hat\pi_0^{E_0}$ (that is, $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2,\widehat{A_0})$ modulo `uvCrossingIdeal`), and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that model, subject to $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$ in $O$, the requirement that $\iota$ carry the image of each element of $A_0$ in $O$ to the corresponding constant `UVCrossingModel.const`, and $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U \cdot \mathtt{U}$, $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V \cdot \mathtt{V}$; and for every valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ containing $O$ which is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$, with $c_x$ in $\mathfrak m_{W_x}$ and $c_y$ not in $\mathfrak m_{W_x}$ (each phrased conditionally on membership in $W_x$): every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ containing $O$ for which the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $\mathfrak m_V$ and $c_y$ does not lie in $\mathfrak m_V$ satisfies $W_x \subseteq V$.
--
--   This is the canonicity, or minimality, statement for the Igusa branch at a node of the semistable reduction of the full-level modular curve: among the valuation subrings of the level field that dominate the node ring $O$, have $\pi_0$ in their maximal ideal and $c_y$ outside it, the branch $W_x$ cut out by $c_x$ is the smallest. It is used by the theorems producing node centres and the layered node rings at Igusa level, where it identifies the branch attached to a node uniquely and so allows branch data to be transported.
